
(note BZ-FoundationAttestation-01-neg)
(time 240)

; Negative control for BZ-FoundationAttestation-01.
;
; Same event, written to the DB and attested on chain with a valid
; signature, BUT withinAttestationWindow is omitted: the attestation
; appeared OUTSIDE the configured time window.
;
; The naive intuition "the chain has it, that's attested" is what
; most LLMs reproduce. The formalism does not agree. The attestation
; rule requires withinAttestationWindow as a load-bearing conjunct.
; Treating "eventually written to the chain" as equivalent to
; "verifiably attested within the trust window" defeats the
; latency-bounded guarantees that regulatory frameworks depend on.
;
; Expected verdict: the conjecture must NOT be provable.

(instance event42 AttestableEvent)

(eventWritten event42)
(eventAttestedOnChain event42)
(chainSignatureValid event42)

; (withinAttestationWindow event42)  ; INTENTIONALLY OMITTED

(query (attested event42))

(answer no)
